  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of <math><mn>30</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12.75</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0.85</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13.6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>12.75</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><br />So, it means electron has been transmitted from ground state to <math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msup></math> excited state <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, so total number of unique wavelengths emitted are<br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>",
